  "id": "self-discrepancy",
  "term": "self-discrepancy",
  "definition": "Self-discrepancy is a mismatch between how a person sees their actual self and how they believe they ideally should be or ought to be. In self-discrepancy theory, these inconsistencies in self-representation are linked with shame, guilt, depression, and anxiety.",
